Remove the manual replace and let `JSON.stringify` handle escaping:
```tsx
export function Layout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  const { rootCssClass, resolvedScheme } = useColorScheme();
  const baseUrl = process.env.OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL ?? "https://omnibridge-dev.vercel.app/api/v1";
  return (
    <html lang="en" suppressHydrationWarning className={rootCssClass} style={{ colorScheme: resolvedScheme }}>
      <head>
        {/* ... */}
        <script
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{
            __html: `window.__OMNIBRIDGE_BASE_URL__ = ${JSON.stringify(baseUrl)};`,
          }}
        />
        {/* ... */}
      </head>
      {/* ... */}
    </html>
  );
}
```

Wrap the route handlers with an authentication guard. For example, create a `requireAuth` loader/action wrapper and apply it to the routes:
```ts
import { requireAuth } from "~/utils/auth";

export default [
  // ... other routes
  route(
    "/api/v1/chat/completions",
    "routes/api.v1.chat.completions.ts",
    { loader: requireAuth, action: requireAuth }
  ),
  route(
    "/api/v1/models",
    "routes/api.v1.models.ts",
    { loader: requireAuth }
  ),
  // ... other routes
] satisfies RouteConfig;
```
Ensure `requireAuth` validates the session (e.g., via Supabase JWT) and returns a 401/403 response when the user is not authorized.

